2. Intel HEXL  —  Apache License 2.0, Copyright (C) 2020 Intel Corporation
   Full text: LICENSE.hexl
   Vendored:  hexl/
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

MODIFICATIONS TO HEXL, stated as required by Apache-2.0 section 4(b):

  a) Only the 8 compute kernels the verifier reaches are vendored
     (eltwise-{add,sub,mult,fma,reduce}-mod, ntt-internal, ntt-radix-2,
     number-theory). Headers are reduced to the set the compiler reports as
     included. Nothing else from upstream is present.

  b) HEXL's CMake build is NOT used. The one header CMake generates,
     include/hexl/util/defines.hpp, is instead hand-written for the GNU,
     non-debug, NON-AVX-512 configuration. HEXL_DEBUG and every HEXL_HAS_AVX512*
     macro are deliberately left undefined.

     ★ This also retires two portability patches Soqucoin previously had to carry
       against HEXL's CMake, both of which hardcoded -march=native and therefore
       compiled for whichever machine happened to run the build. Not using that
       build system removes the problem rather than patching around it.

  c) Two upstream dependencies are REPLACED BY SHIMS in hexl/shim/, which are
     Soqucoin-original and are the only original code in this directory:

       cpuinfo_x86.h    replaces Google cpu_features. HEXL's kernels include it
                        unconditionally to runtime-dispatch AVX-512 paths. No
                        AVX-512 kernel is compiled here, so reporting every
                        feature absent is the only consistent answer rather than
                        a simplification. It also makes the dispatch a
                        compile-time constant, which matters because upstream
                        consults the environment variables HEXL_DISABLE_AVX512DQ,
                        HEXL_DISABLE_AVX512IFMA and HEXL_DISABLE_AVX512VBMI2 —
                        an environment variable must never be able to change
                        consensus behaviour.

       easylogging++.h  replaces easyloggingpp. HEXL's logging.hpp includes it
                        unconditionally, but with HEXL_DEBUG off every logging
                        macro expands to nothing, so the real library would be
                        compiled in purely to be unused.

     Vendoring both upstream libraries instead would have added several thousand
     lines of third-party code to the review surface for code that cannot run.

  d) `src/eltwise/eltwise-reduce-mod.cpp` guards its include of
     `eltwise-reduce-mod-avx512.hpp`. That header reaches `util/avx512-util.hpp`, which
     includes `<immintrin.h>` unconditionally and therefore broke every non-x86 build, while
     every USE of the symbols it declares was already inside `#ifdef HEXL_HAS_AVX512DQ` or
     `IFMA` in that file. The include is now guarded to match the uses. The other seven
     kernels needed no change: their avx512 headers are pure declarations with no intrinsics.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Soqucoin's own contribution
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Soqucoin's intellectual property in this subsystem is the RELATION and its
policy — corrector-chain pins, ring-degree headroom, dual-target verifiable
encryption, H_lat (SOQ-P010 / SOQ-P011) — and the consensus rules around it. It
is NOT the proof system, which is IBM's. Nothing in this directory belongs in the
Soqucoin-original column of ATTRIBUTION.md.
